research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-56-{"id":"fs-continuous-image-of-a-closed-set-is-closed","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.mit.edu/classes/18.100/100B.S1-Lects.html"],"rationale":"The MIT notes distinguish compact-image preservation from closed-image preservation. The local refutation uses the standard closed domain [1,infinity) under reciprocal, whose image is (0,1].","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-57-{"id":"fs-evt-holds-on-every-bounded-domain","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://uoe-school-of-mathematics.github.io/MATH08081_IMA/Ch4.S9.html"],"rationale":"The source explains that EVT needs a closed bounded interval and that open intervals can lose attained extrema. The local witness is the identity on (0,1).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-58-{"id":"ex-distance-to-the-integers-is-1-lipschitz","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.math.uchicago.edu/~shmuel/QuantCourse%20/Metric%20Space/Heinonen%2C%20Lecs%20on%20Lip%20Analysis.pdf"],"rationale":"Heinonen states that distance to any set is 1-Lipschitz. The local example specializes to the integers and adds the exact range [0,1/2] and zero set.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-59-{"id":"cex-dirichlet-is-nowhere-continuous","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Analysis/Mathematical_Analysis_%28Zakon%29/04%3A_Function_Limits_and_Continuity/4.01%3A_Basic_Definitions"],"rationale":"Zakon gives exactly the rational indicator and proves that it is discontinuous at every real because rationals and irrationals meet every neighbourhood. The local proof is the same density argument.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-60-{"id":"ex-x-times-dirichlet-is-continuous-exactly-at-zero","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Analysis/Real_Analysis_%28Boman_and_Rogers%29/06%3A_Continuity_-_What_It_Isnt_and_What_It_Is/6.01%3A_An_Analytic_De%EF%AC%81nition_of_Continuity"],"rationale":"The open text states exactly that x times the rational indicator is continuous at zero and nowhere else. The local proof expands both cases without sequences.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
