research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-product-of-uniformly-continuous-functions-need-not-be-uniformly-continuous.log-6-BOUNDARY: The domain A = ℝ has no endpoints; the zero case (x = x′) is automatically handled by the uniform-continuity estimate (|x − x′| = 0 < ε). The counterexample for the square uses distinct points a_k ≠ b_k for every k ∈ ℕ, so no degenerate choice is required. The Archimedean property guarantees that for any δ > 0 an index k can be chosen with |a_k − b_k| < δ while the difference of squares exceeds 2. Hence the refutation is effective for all positive δ.
