research/audit/wave8-preserved-refuters/cex-x-squared-is-not-uniformly-continuous-on-r--e4fd9e3298f77c70.log-6-BOUNDARY: The index shift (k+1) ensures a_0=1, b_0=2, avoiding division by zero at the first index. The pair distance 1/(k+1) is positive for every k and tends to zero. The domain ℝ has no endpoints; the witness pairs lie inside ℝ. The Archimedean estimate in step 3.1 produces an m (and therefore k) for any given δ, and the inequality 1/(k+1) < 1/m < δ is valid by basic order properties. The negation of uniform continuity is correctly applied with ε0=2. No empty-domain, zero, degenerate, or nonempty-choice issues arise.
