research/audit/wave8-preserved-refuters/cex-x-squared-is-not-uniformly-continuous-on-r--e4fd9e3298f77c70.prompt.md-171-4.1 So no real $\delta > 0$ serves $\varepsilon_0 = 2$, and by [L1] the function $f$ is not uniformly continuous on $\mathbb{R}$, although by step 1.1 it is continuous there: the refuted claim is false. [step 1.1, step 3.1, L1, L5] ∎
